Title: NICK AND ME
Credit: adapted from the book
Author: Short Film Adaptation

[[WITHHELD NAME RULE: Narrator's given name is not spoken or shown until final moments.]]

FADE IN:

=== S01 - KIRK STREET APT ===

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY

A fifth-floor walk-up. Brick city light through old windows. MA sits in an overstuffed chair under an afghan, game show murmuring. Pills lined on the kitchen counter.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Not the book. My real Big Brother.

NICK fills the doorway—scarred brow, chin mark, hair uncombed, boots heavy. The room seems smaller.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Nick was the guy everybody was scared of. A modern-day warrior. I lived with him and Ma after dad took off when I was about eight.

Nick checks Ma, then pins the NARRATOR with a look that is care and command mixed.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Someone has to be here with Ma. She’s getting older and it’s hard for her to see.

=== S02 - PIZZA SIDEWALK ===

EXT. PIZZA PLACE SIDEWALK - DAY

Narrator approaches the front door. A YOUNG WOMAN with short brown hair, black V-neck, jeans, blue tennis shoes, backpack, fish-symbol necklace—trips on cement and brushes his shoulder.

They steady. A look. Her eyes are light blue, early-morning sky.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
The first thing I did was ask if she was okay. She said yes. She said her name was Sionna.

She declines pizza, offers coffee sometime, moves away smooth as water—looks back over her shoulder.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
It was like I knew her. Like the tide coming in. I didn’t want to move my feet.

=== S03 - JAVA HUT ===

INT. THE JAVA HUT - DAY

Back table near the wall. Backpacks. Student noise. SIONNA waits in a loose green hooded top. Narrator sits. The room falls away in her gaze.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
She had a degree in English. She talked about Wuthering Heights—ghosts, double characters, the moors. A love that never changes will destroy you.

Something in him wakes. They lean closer over coffee. Life outside the glass looks different when he leaves.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
She made me feel smarter just by being around her. We made another date. I couldn’t wait.

=== S04 - KIRK STREET APT ===

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY

Ma’s eyes glassy, empty for a beat—searching for church, for a neighbor long unseen. Narrator steadies her toward the day’s pill box.

NICK erupts—missed doctor, priorities, money fear of nursing homes. His fists open and close. Door SLAMS.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
God, sometimes I really hate Nick inside. He’s done so much for us. And I’m tired of his shit. I would never tell anybody that.

=== S05 - JOE'S BAR ===

INT. JOE'S BAR AND GRILL - NIGHT

Smoke, rock, pool room hush spreading. Nick’s temper finds an old flame’s new man. Crowd tightens. Narrator steps into Nick’s rage—closer than he has ever dared.

Time thins. Nick’s fist draws back toward his little brother’s face. Bouncers crash in. Chaos.

EXT. MILWAUKEE STREET - CONTINUOUS

Narrator RUNS—lungs raw, cold air—toward the only person who feels like home.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I found myself running to Sionna. Into the arms of the only person I felt I could trust.

=== S06 - POLICE STATION ===

INT. POLICE STATION - DAY

Ancient stone. A counter. An OFFICER’s mouth moving. Narrator’s hands shake on a cup of water.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
They were hit broadside. My brother in serious condition. My mother passed away at the scene.

The words hollow the air. He cannot yet go look at Nick.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Nick killed her. He fucking killed my mom.

=== S07 - SIONNA DUPLEX ===

INT. SIONNA'S DUPLEX - NIGHT

Knock. Sionna opens a crack—then Nick is inside, towering, blaming her for school, for Ma, for his ruined name. He backs her to the hallway wall. A switchblade opens.

The front door hits the wall. Narrator bursts in—grabs—struggle—

Steel finds flesh. Red on wood. Sionna sinks. Nick elbows free, wipes the blade, flees into dark.

Narrator on the floor, hands stacked on the wound, voice breaking toward a phone, sirens rising.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
My brother stabbed her. If I hadn’t held on, she would have died in that hallway.

=== S08 - SEATTLE ===

EXT. SEATTLE STREET - DAY (YEARS LATER)

Gray blanket sky. Mist. Narrator older, walking alone past market noise and hooded strangers. A dark-haired woman ahead stings memory—then is not her.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Many years had passed since my Milwaukee days. I had my own chain of pizzerias in the Northwest. Seven years of loneliness. Seven years of hatred for my brother.

He stops. Breath. A decision lands clean.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I had to see Nick. I had to put this behind me forever.

=== S09 - PRISON VISIT ===

INT. GREEN BAY CORRECTIONAL - VISIT BOOTH - DAY

Plexiglass. Phones. NICK enters older, thinner, gray at the sides, eyes bagged and sad. They sit. They look.

Narrator speaks—years of held truth: control, the crash, the knife, the life taken from him. Then the turn.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I forgive you. I forgive you for being a huge asshole because it sets me free. It releases your control over me forever.

Nick’s tears hit the ledge. Soft broken apology. A guard signals time. Nick is led away.

Narrator hangs up the yellow receiver. Sits in the quiet. On his way out, almost to himself—

NARRATOR
(whisper)
That’s me. President Peter Olson.

FADE OUT.

END.
